\begin_inset Formula $t \in [\text{2009-05-01T00:00:00Z}, \text{2009-07-01T00:00:00Z})$
\end_inset

. The minimum timestamp is 
\family typewriter
2009-05-01 00:00:00
\family default
. 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
All models, IDF vocabularies, user profiles, and collaborative factors are fitted strictly on data preceding the respective evaluation partition. Evaluable test users are defined as those possessing at least one ground-truth interaction in 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{D}_{\text{test}}$
\end_inset

, yielding exactly 
\begin_inset Formula $|\mathcal{U}_{\text{test}}| = 518$
\end_inset

 evaluable test users. During evaluation, all items previously observed by user 
\begin_inset Formula $u$
\end_inset

 in 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{D}_{\text{train}} \cup \mathcal{D}_{\text{val}}$
\end_inset

 are masked (
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{r}_{ui} = -\infty$
\end_inset

), enforcing pure novel-item discovery.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
System Architecture and Methodology
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The overall system architecture comprises three independent retrieval and scoring streams unified by the Global Normalized Arbiter, as depicted in the mathematical formulations below.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Implicit MSVD Collaborative Model
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The collaborative stream models the interaction matrix 
\begin_inset Formula $R \in \mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{U}| \times |\mathcal{I}|}$
\end_inset

 derived from training play counts. For each user-item pair 
\begin_inset Formula $(u, i)$
\end_inset

, we define the binary preference 
\begin_inset Formula $p_{ui}$
\end_inset

 and confidence 
\begin_inset Formula $c_{ui}$
\end_inset

 via logarithmic scaling: 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
p_{ui} = \mathbb{I}(r_{ui} > 0),
\end{equation}
\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
c_{ui} = 1 + \kappa \ln(1 + r_{ui}),
\end{equation}
\end_inset

where 
\begin_inset Formula $\kappa = 40.0$
\end_inset

 governs confidence expansion. The latent user factors 
\begin_inset Formula $X \in \mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{U}| \times K}$
\end_inset

 and item factors 
\begin_inset Formula $Y \in \mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{I}| \times K}$
\end_inset

 (with 
\begin_inset Formula $K = 64$
\end_inset

) are estimated by minimizing the weighted L2 regularized objective: 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
\mathcal{L}(X, Y) = \sum_{u=1}^{|\mathcal{U}|} \sum_{i=1}^{|\mathcal{I}|} c_{ui} \left( p_{ui} - x_u^T y_i \right)^2 + \lambda \left( \sum_{u=1}^{|\mathcal{U}|} \|x_u\|_2^2 + \sum_{i=1}^{|\mathcal{I}|} \|y_i\|_2^2 \right),
\end{equation}
\end_inset

where 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda = 0.05$
\end_inset

 is the regularization parameter. Optimization is executed via Alternating Least Squares across 10 complete iterations. The raw collaborative score for user 
\begin_inset Formula $u$
\end_inset

 and item 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

 is computed as: 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
s_{ui}^{\text{msvd}} = x_u^T y_i.
\end{equation}
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Stream A: Artist-Tag Semantic Fusion
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Stream A incorporates external semantic knowledge from the HetRec 2011 social tagging dataset. After filtering rare tags, a vocabulary of 
\begin_inset Formula $|\mathcal{V}| = 2,299$
\end_inset

 tags is retained. Each candidate track 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

 is associated with its artist's tag frequency distribution. The term frequency 
\begin_inset Formula $\text{TF}(i, t)$
\end_inset

 and inverse document frequency 
\begin_inset Formula $\text{IDF}(t)$
\end_inset

 are computed as: 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
\text{TF}(i, t) = \frac{\text{freq}(i, t)}{\sum_{t' \in \mathcal{V}} \text{freq}(i, t')},
\end{equation}
\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
\text{IDF}(t) = \ln \left( \frac{1 + |\mathcal{I}|}{1 + \text{DF}(t)} \right) + 1,
\end{equation}
\end_inset

where 
\begin_inset Formula $\text{DF}(t)$
\end_inset

 is the document frequency of tag 
\begin_inset Formula $t$
\end_inset

 across the candidate catalog. The normalized item tag vector 
\begin_inset Formula $t_i \in \mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{V}|}$
\end_inset

 is defined as: 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
t_i = \frac{\text{TF-IDF}(i)}{\|\text{TF-IDF}(i)\|_2}.
\end{equation}
\end_inset

For user 
\begin_inset Formula $u$
\end_inset

, a semantic preference profile 
\begin_inset Formula $z_u \in \mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{V}|}$
\end_inset

 is constructed by projecting the user's training confidence vector 
\begin_inset Formula $C_u \in \mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{I}|}$
\end_inset

 onto the item-tag matrix 
\begin_inset Formula $T \in \mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{I}| \times |\mathcal{V}|}$
\end_inset

: 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
z_u = \frac{C_u T}{\|C_u T\|_2}.
\end{equation}
\end_inset

The semantic affinity score is then computed via sparse vector-matrix multiplication: 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
s_{ui}^{\text{tag}} = z_u^T t_i.
\end{equation}
\end_inset

In our catalog, 
\begin_inset Formula $594,225$
\end_inset

 tracks (
\begin_inset Formula $39.7824\%$
\end_inset

) possess non-zero tag representations, containing 
\begin_inset Formula $11,920,822$
\end_inset

 non-zero entries in sparse CSR format.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Stream B: Temporal Recency Preference Modeling
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Stream B captures short-term listening momentum and preference recency. For each user-item interaction 
\begin_inset Formula $(u, i)$
\end_inset

 observed at timestamp 
\begin_inset Formula $t_{ui}$
\end_inset

, the temporal affinity score is computed using an exponential decay kernel: 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
S_{ui}^{\text{temp}} = c_{ui} \exp\left( -\gamma \Delta t_{ui} \right),
\end{equation}
\end_inset

where 
\begin_inset Formula $\gamma = 0.10\text{ day}^{-1}$
\end_inset

, and 
\begin_inset Formula $\Delta t_{ui} = (t_{\text{ref}} - t_{ui})$
\end_inset

 represents the elapsed time in days relative to the reference cutoff timestamp 
\begin_inset Formula $t_{\text{ref}}$
\end_inset

 (strictly set to the start of the evaluation period to prevent leakage). The user's temporal score vector is L2-normalized: 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
s_{u}^{\text{temp}} = \frac{S_u^{\text{temp}}}{\|S_u^{\text{temp}}\|_2}.
\end{equation}
\end_inset

The temporal matrix spans 
\begin_inset Formula $4,009,238$
\end_inset

 non-zero entries across the candidate space.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Global Normalized Multi-Stream Arbiter
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Because the raw MSVD collaborative dot-products 
\begin_inset Formula $s_{ui}^{\text{msvd}} \in (-\infty, \infty)$
\end_inset

 have unconstrained variance across users, while 
\begin_inset Formula $s_{ui}^{\text{tag}}, s_{ui}^{\text{temp}} \in [0, 1]$
\end_inset

, naive linear combination creates severe distortion. To establish scale compatibility, we apply per-user min-max normalization to the collaborative stream: 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
\tilde{s}_{ui}^{\text{msvd}} = \frac{s_{ui}^{\text{msvd}} - \min_{j \in \mathcal{I}} s_{uj}^{\text{msvd}}}{\max_{j \in \mathcal{I}} s_{uj}^{\text{msvd}} - \min_{j \in \mathcal{I}} s_{uj}^{\text{msvd}}}.
\end{equation}
\end_inset

The final composite ranking score 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{r}_{ui}$
\end_inset

 is produced via global weighted multi-stream arbitration: 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
\hat{r}_{ui} = w_{\text{msvd}} \tilde{s}_{ui}^{\text{msvd}} + w_{\text{tag}} \tilde{s}_{ui}^{\text{tag}} + w_{\text{temp}} \tilde{s}_{ui}^{\text{temp}},
\end{equation}
\end_inset

with locked global weights determined on the validation set: 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
w_{\text{msvd}} = 0.20, \quad w_{\text{tag}} = 0.30, \quad w_{\text{temp}} = 0.50.
\end{equation}
\end_inset

All candidate items previously seen in training are masked: 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
\hat{r}_{ui} \leftarrow -\infty \quad \forall i \in \mathcal{H}_u.
\end{equation}
\end_inset

The top-
\begin_inset Formula $K$
\end_inset

 recommendations are retrieved via exact partial sorting (
\family typewriter
numpy.argpartition
\family default
) over all 
\begin_inset Formula $1,493,688$
\end_inset

 candidate items without approximate nearest-neighbor approximations.
\end_layout

