\begin_inset Formula $p = 0.0263, d = 0.1235$
\end_inset

), and MAP@10 (
\begin_inset Formula $p = 0.0447, d = 0.1119$
\end_inset

). 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Global Arbiter vs.
\begin_inset space \space{}

\end_inset

Base MSVD:
\series default
 While the Arbiter achieves a 
\begin_inset Formula $+16.384\%$
\end_inset

 descriptive gain in NDCG@10 (
\begin_inset Formula $0.007414$
\end_inset

 vs.
\begin_inset space \space{}

\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $0.006370$
\end_inset

), the paired Wilcoxon test yields 
\begin_inset Formula $p = 0.7292$
\end_inset

 (
\begin_inset Formula $W = 201.5, d = 0.0212$
\end_inset

). Therefore, this improvement is characterized strictly as a 
\series bold
descriptive and practical empirical improvement
\series default
, rather than a statistically significant shift under strict hypothesis testing. 
\end_layout

