\begin_layout Standard
While the Popularity baseline suffers from extreme redundancy (recommending only 
\begin_inset Formula $90$
\end_inset

 distinct tracks and 
\begin_inset Formula $38$
\end_inset

 artists with a high pairwise Jaccard similarity of 
\begin_inset Formula $0.6030$
\end_inset

), the Global Normalized Arbiter recommends 
\begin_inset Formula $6,118$
\end_inset

 unique tracks with high recommendation entropy (
\begin_inset Formula $12.20\text{ bits}$
\end_inset

) and low inter-user redundancy (pairwise Jaccard 
\begin_inset Formula $= 0.0021$
\end_inset

). Furthermore, the Arbiter surfaces items deeper in the long tail, increasing average popularity rank to 
\begin_inset Formula $21,542$
\end_inset

 (compared to 
\begin_inset Formula $9,614$
\end_inset

 for Base MSVD).
\end_layout

