\begin_layout Section
Explainability Framework
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A key operational advantage of the Global Normalized Arbiter is intrinsic linear explainability. Because each candidate score 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{r}_{ui}$
\end_inset

 is a linear combination of normalized components, the system outputs exact percentage attribution for any recommended track: 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
\text{Contrib}_{\text{stream}}(u, i) = \frac{w_{\text{stream}} \tilde{s}_{ui}^{\text{stream}}}{\hat{r}_{ui}} \times 100\%.
\end{equation}
\end_inset

For example, a recommended track can be explicitly justified to the user: 
\shape italic

\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Recommended because of 42% Collaborative Pattern Match, 35% Match with your top tags (indie rock, electronic), and 23% Recent Artist Affinity.
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset


\shape default

\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Discussion
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The empirical findings provide several critical insights for large-scale recommendation: 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Normalization as an Enabler of Hybrid Fusion:
\series default
 The failure of unnormalized fixed fusion (
\begin_inset Formula $0.005932$
\end_inset

 NDCG@10) versus the success of the Global Normalized Arbiter (
\begin_inset Formula $0.007414$
\end_inset

) demonstrates that raw collaborative dot-products cannot be combined additively with bounded auxiliary scores without per-user calibration. 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Auxiliary Strengths in Sparse Cohorts:
\series default
 The 
\begin_inset Formula $+50.472\%$
\end_inset

 descriptive gain in low-activity users (
\begin_inset Formula $0.017421$
\end_inset

 vs.
\begin_inset space \space{}

\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $0.011578$
\end_inset

) highlights that social tags and temporal recency kernels compensate effectively for sparse collaborative factor profiles. 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Rigorous Evaluation Realism:
\series default
 Evaluating across the unpruned 
\begin_inset Formula $1.49\text{M}$
\end_inset

 candidate catalog reflects true production conditions. The low absolute magnitude of NDCG (
\begin_inset Formula $0.0074$
\end_inset

) is typical for full-catalog ranking without candidate pre-filtering
\begin_inset space ~

\end_inset


